Chapter: GroupServiceCount
  cites Net chapter GroupMembership
  cites Foreword chapter Maybe

 The service registry's count must equal the list it counts. That invariant
 broke on 2026-08-19 and nothing here could see it: `gs-register-service` read
 `list-length deduped + 1` AFTER pushing onto `deduped`, and `list-push` had
 already extended it in place, so one registered service reported two. The
 next `gs-find-service` walked to index 1 of a one-element list and took the
 bounds trap, EXC=06.

 THIS ARM EXISTS BECAUSE THE ONE THAT FOUND IT IS NOT RUN BY ANYTHING.
 `apps/nettool/tests/TestGroupMembership.codex` covers it and lives under
 `apps/`, where `build.ps1`'s app-sweep phase COMPILES every entry chapter and
 runs none of them, so a runtime trap there is invisible to every gate. This
 file is in `codex/test/apps`, which `test.ps1` sweeps wholesale and actually
 executes.

 The count is printed beside the length rather than compared here, so the
 `.expected` carries both numbers and a future drift names itself instead of
 reporting a bare False.

 We say:

Section: Fixtures

  web-1 : ServiceLocation = svc-location-new "web" "1.0" "node-1" "10.0.2.15" 80 SrPrimary
  db-2 : ServiceLocation = svc-location-new "db" "1.0" "node-2" "10.0.2.16" 5432 SrPrimary

Section: The Invariant

 One service: the count and the list must both say one. A second, different
 service: both say two. Re-registering the SAME service from the same member
 must dedup, so both still say two rather than three -- that arm is what makes
 this a test of the count rather than of the push.

  base : GroupState = group-new "g" "node-1"
  one : GroupState = gs-register-service base web-1
  two : GroupState = gs-register-service one db-2
  again : GroupState = gs-register-service two web-1

  row : Text, GroupState -> Text
  row (label) (st) =
    label & " count=" & show (st.gs-service-count) & " len=" & show (list-length (st.gs-services))

Section: Entry

 `gs-find-service` is called last because it is the reader that trapped: it
 walks `0` to `gs-service-count`, so a count larger than the list faults here
 rather than quietly returning a wrong answer.

  found : GroupState, Text -> Integer
  found (st) (name) = list-length (gs-find-service st name)

  opening : [Console] Nothing = act
    print-line-uni (row "one  " one)
    print-line-uni (row "two  " two)
    print-line-uni (row "again" again)
    print-line-uni ("find web=" & show (found again "web") & " db=" & show (found again "db"))
  end
